description: DaisyUI multi-brand themes (agentlabs | timerich)
globs: "**/*.{css,tsx}"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Styling

- Themes: DaisyUI `agentlabs` and `timerich` only — set `data-theme` from the resolved brand (`brand.theme`), never hardcode one brand in shared components
- Prefer DaisyUI semantic utilities: `btn-primary`, `bg-base-100`, `text-base-content`, `border-base-300`
- Agent Labs accent is lime → `primary` / `accent`; Time Rich tokens live under the `timerich` theme once defined in `app/globals.css`
- Errors → `error`
- For custom CSS outside DaisyUI, use theme/`--brand-*` tokens from `app/globals.css` (or brand-specific variables under each DaisyUI theme block)
- Do not hardcode hex colors in components when a theme/brand token exists
- Do not invent themes beyond `agentlabs` and `timerich`

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<html data-theme={brand.theme}>
<button className="btn btn-primary">Join</button>
<p className="text-base-content/70">Muted copy</p>

// ❌ BAD
<html data-theme="agentlabs"> {/* hardcoded in shared root when brand varies */}
<button className="bg-[#d4ff4f] text-[#0b0b10]">Join</button>
```
